### Coverage lift

Pass 1 covered: 2-WL serial + small-scale parallel (4 procs), 3-WL on
chiatta00 single-node MPI. Pass 2 adds 5 explicit claim groundings,
including paper-Table-1 dataset grounding and the textbook 2-WL/3-WL
expressivity hierarchy (Rook/Shrikhande), which directly grounds §7's
"expressivity equivalence" claim and the motivation for pushing k up.

### Still out of scope on free CPU

- Multi-node distributed runs on a Cray (the headline scaling figure).
- 2,193× single-node-single-core speedup vs K-WL baseline on 662_bus
  (requires building K-WL baseline binary; CPU-bound but unrelated to
  ScaWL correctness). 662_bus has n=662 and at our pure-Python pace
  one 2-WL iteration on n=662 is ~ (662/60)² × 0.27 s ≈ 33 s, which
  is feasible but not informative without the K-WL baseline binary.

